   "text": "September 16th, 1992. By 9 a.m., the Bank of England had already spent more than a billion pounds buying back its own currency. At 11, it raised interest rates from 10 to 12 percent. At 2:15, it promised 15. In the money markets, overnight cash was quoted at 100 percent."
  },
